window.products.push({"id":839092,"name":"Replacement Lid Knobs for Revere Ware Lids (two knobs)","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":13.49,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zDOrONv7L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Keep your Revere Ware cookware looking great with a new replacement Bakelite lid knob from RevereWareParts!  These replacement knobs are made specifically for Revere Ware lids with the built in screw, and look and work just like the originals.  SOME IMPORTANT DETAILS  - NO SCREW IS INCLUDED; Revere Ware lids a screw attachhed to the knob.  - The knobs are made from Bakelite with a brass nut insert. - If you want to use this knob with a lid that does not have a screw (sometimes they break off) you need a stainless or brass 8-32 machine screw between .25 and .35 in long. - The knobs are 1.7 in (43 mm) diameter, 0.7 in (18 mm) tall.  - Will fit all Revere Ware lids, vintage era and newer that have a similar looking knob. This knob may not fit Revere Ware lid styles that have a different looking knob.   FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS Will the knobs work on Rena Ware cookware?No, these are made for Revere Ware not Rena Ware.  Are the knobs oven safe?  No, the knobs are not safe to use in an oven. Most modern ovens, even when set for a safe temperature, will reach higher temperatures in areas that can damage Bakelite parts.  Are the knobs dishwasher safe? Repeated washing in a dishwasher will dull the finish of Bakelite pieces.   Will these knobs fit any other cookware brands? These knobs are made only for the specific Revere Ware types above and are not made to fit any other types or brands of cookware.   What other Revere Ware replacement parts are available? We also sell a number of other replacement parts made for Revere Ware cookware. You can find our complete list of items available on Amazon.com by clicking on our name under the Buy Now button and selecting the Products tab.  TROUBLESHOOTING  If you see something like an eraser head instead of a screw on your lid, it is the nut insert from the old knob; unscrew it with pliers to expose the screw.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zDOrONv7L._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"LYWINDODO","source_asin":"B001U2N6YY","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-839092","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B001U2N6YY","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B001U2N6YY","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
